      "project_health": "Green 7/13/26: | The project has successfully transitioned into the testing phase, with core processes configured to a level that supports system testing activities. IC continues to provide support during testing sessions while client staff actively participate in both guided and independent testing efforts. Overall project engagement remains strong, and testing activities are progressing as planned. The primary outstanding dependency is the DCT from client. Additional data quality issues were identified by conversion following the latest DCT (2nd attempt) submission, and resolution is required before the conversion can begin Pass 1 mapping activities. As a result, conversion timelines and related deliverable dates cannot yet be finalized. Further updates are expected once the outstanding DCT issues have been addressed. 6/9/26: | Testing training has been completed. IC provided the client with test guides, and showed client how to use the tracker | Items have been added to tracker, and IC started resolving Tyler-owned items in the tracker. | A Bluebeam issue was identified and has since been resolved. | IC is working to obtain an answer regarding the TCM integration. | IC worked last week to get the TCM integration setup. IC owes client an answer for generating the Master PW- still working on this | ESR is expected to be coming down the pipeline soon. To help the client get ahead of the process, IC worked with the client to complete preliminary ESR-to-EPL setup activities. | The project is currently targeting a January go-live date (preferably mid-Jan to allow staff time to adjust following the holiday break) | The team is working to align on DCT completion, and Amy is actively working to get this finalized. An ETA has not yet been provided. Once the DCT is uploaded, we can begin planning and scheduling conversion activities. | Conversion engineer has been assigned, Bennett | The city confirmed that SMEs and Amy will have availability to complete data validation activities. | The city also confirmed SME availability to support testing efforts. | The configuration phase is progressing as planned and remains within scope. | IC is working to finalize/cleanup and complete Tyler owned processes by the end of the week. | Melanie created a ticket for report toolkit access to be deployed- this may need to be a case for TSM- I will get clarification on this 4/1/26- Current Focus: Finalizing Atlas questionnaires (all departments except Department of Works complete) | Determining path forward for conversion (traditional vs. data archive) | Preparing for configuring processes Key Updates: Process ownership being agreed by April 3; Tyler will own Building 10 (possibly 11), client will own remainder | Kyle to begin configuration of Tyler-owned processes April 10; Kyle to provide configuration support during week of April 14 and again week of April 28 | Client evaluating conversion path; multiple data sources (approx. 3) pose risk for traditional conversion (some are on spreadsheets!)- this was a surprise to sales while on call (contract only has for 1 source) | Target go-live: January 2027; implementation plan laid out, but timeline tight with only three conversion passes and strict milestones | Conversion decision expected from client by April 28 (next steering committee meeting) | Internal client disorganization observed; alignment on processes and potential duplication issues noted | Payments quote signed; next steps coordinated by sales | Bluebeam quote signed; client working on license setup | Process count still uncertain; potentially 100+ processes | During steering meeting, they asked if their IT folks could help configure Risks / Issues: Significant staff effort required if traditional conversion pursued | Tight timeline and dependency on client\u2019s ability to configure processes correctly and by due date we\u2019ve laid out | High risk if milestones missed; delay beyond June 15 for conversion start increases scope risk | Lack of internal discussions on how each dept is building, to avoid duplications and how to manage that- this could also impact validation Next Steps: Confirm process ownership and finalize Atlas questionnaires by April 3 | Receive client decision on conversion path by April 28 | Begin configuration support week of April 14 and April 28 | Coordinate payments and Bluebeam setup | Monitor process count and complexity to adjust risk mitigation",
